{"seconds": 75.5, "exit": 0, "final": "**Move 2: White plays Qxd4**\n\n**Move 3: Bxf5** - Black takes the knight\n\n**Move 4: White's best try is Qxd5**\n\n**Move 5: Bxd5** - Black takes the queen\n\nThis wins Black a queen for a knight and pawn. That's the key tactical blow!\n\nPerfect. The move is **Nxd4+** and the main line is **Nxd4+ Qxd4 Bxf5 Qxd5 Bxd5** with a decisive material advantage for Black.\n\nThe motif is a **fork** - the knight on d4 gives check and attacks multiple pieces (king, queen, and the c2 pawn), and even though White captures with the queen, the follow-up Bxf5 and Qxd5 Bxd5 wins the queen.\n\nActually, more precisely, it's an **attraction** or **deflection** - the knight forces the queen to d4 where it can be attacked, and the bishop then captures on f5 attacking the queen, leading to a winning sequence.\n\nOr even better: it's a forcing **fork** pattern where the knight check initiates a tactical sequence.\n\n<json>\n{\"move\": \"Nxd4+\", \"line\": [\"Nxd4+\", \"Qxd4\", \"Bxf5\", \"Qxd5\", \"Bxd5\", \"Rxf5\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"attraction\"]}\n</json>\n\n**Coaching Note:**\n\nWhen the opponent hangs a pawn, don't just recapture material - look for forcing moves with multiple threats. Nxd4+ checks the king while attacking the queen and c2 pawn. After Qxd4, your bishop takes the knight with tempo, and when White tries Qxd5, you capture the queen with Bxd5, winning a queen for just a knight and pawn. Always calculate forcing sequences several moves deep.", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "k2qr3/pp4p1/2nBb2p/3pPN1P/P1pP4/2P3P1/2PQK3/5R2 b - - 0 25"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "k2qr3/pp4p1/2nBb2p/3pPN1P/P1pP4/2P3P1/2PQK3/5R2 b - - 0 25"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "k2qr3/pp4p1/2nBb2p/3pPN1P/P1pP4/2P3P1/2PQK3/5R2 b - - 0 25"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "k2qr3/pp4p1/2nBb2p/3pPN1P/P1pP4/2